# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the IPMI BMC simulator on UDP 0.0.0.0:623 (no
# firewall) then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the vulnerable service is ALREADY LISTENING on all interfaces when the
#     agent starts (a do-nothing agent must fail the firewall check);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so nothing a solution does can kill the box.
#
# The primary, LIVE control is the iptables restriction on UDP/623 (read from
# the running kernel table). The cipher-suite config edit is a defence-in-depth
# assertion; the simulator does not enforce cipher suites, so it is verified as
# config state only. There is no daemon-restart step for the firewall control.
